# Nested sub-callee that needs a real instance — refused (échte creatie)

The nested-Invoke refinement (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3a, 2026-08-25) lowers a declared
subscope inside a per-element callee ONLY when its own callee also passes the
purity analysis — that is function composition. `InnerConflict`'s output is a
root-level unordered group of two OVERLAPPING conditions with no unconditional
base: a conflict-bearing group whose §9.5 conflict channel needs a STANDING
instance, not a function. So `KamerCreatie.bedrag = inner.y` refuses at the
nested read — real creation (a conflict channel / roles / ladders on the
instance) stays Direction B.

```catala
declaration scope InnerConflict:
  input x content integer
  output y content integer

scope InnerConflict:
  definition y under condition x > 0 consequence equals x + 1
  definition y under condition x > 5 consequence equals x + 2

declaration scope KamerCreatie:
  input grondslag content integer
  inner scope InnerConflict
  output bedrag content integer

scope KamerCreatie:
  definition inner.x equals grondslag
  definition bedrag equals inner.y

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  output totaal content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition totaal equals
    combine all b
      among (map each g among grondslagen to (output of KamerCreatie with { -- grondslag: g }).bedrag)
      in acc initially 0 with (acc + b)
```
